WEBVTT

00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:15,870
Dr. Cutters, on my call today, I checked my last Syrex, and I saw cashews,

00:00:15,870 --> 00:00:21,870
Vasylid, are these the same as raw organic, have Vasylid?

00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:26,270
These were not listed out of range, but are listed under the equivocal.

00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:31,510
What does that mean? Not a good idea to eat? It was 1.69.

00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:37,470
Okay, if I read bed burr correctly, that Syrex array 10.

00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:45,470
So Syrex array 10 is testing 100 or so foods, some cooked, some raw,

00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:50,190
because cooking some foods changes the protein in the food.

00:00:50,190 --> 00:00:57,310
So you could actually have antibodies to cook something and not to raw something.

00:00:57,310 --> 00:01:12,270
But with the nuts, the question is, do cashews, Vasylid, have, do raw organic, have Vasylid?

00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:20,430
I'd say yes, they do, but the test that you did, it is now August, the test that you did,

00:01:20,430 --> 00:01:26,910
I think was in January, you could basically throw this out, because if you've been

00:01:26,910 --> 00:01:35,470
away from cashews for several months, it's a very good chance that you don't have those antibodies

00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:40,110
anymore. So if you have self antibodies, let's say you have antibodies to your thyroid gland,

00:01:40,110 --> 00:01:45,550
so we did a test on you, a complete thyroid profile, let's say you have thyroid globular antibodies,

00:01:46,270 --> 00:01:52,990
common antibody to have, therefore you have an autoimmune disorder that's attacking your thyroid,

00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:56,510
and you have to be careful of certain things, and not eat bloated and all this stuff,

00:01:56,510 --> 00:02:02,510
and I have all this information about autoimmune thyroid called Hashimoto's on our autoimmune course.

00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:07,790
But the music, this is an example. You can have those antibodies your whole life, no matter how well

00:02:07,790 --> 00:02:13,230
you eat, no matter how well you support your thyroid, those antibodies may never go away.

00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:21,390
But with foods, if you stay away from a food for a period of time, the majority of foods,

00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:27,310
those antibodies will dissipate. They're not going to stay around. You know, you always will have

00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:34,270
a thyroid, okay? So you could always have antibodies against it if you developed an autoimmune disease

00:02:34,270 --> 00:02:39,790
against your thyroid. You don't always have cashews in your body. So if you stay away from cashews,

00:02:40,510 --> 00:02:45,150
your B cells aren't going to be continuing to make antibodies against them, that's a whole idea

00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:51,870
of eliminating those from your diet, and those can dissipate, almost always dissipate.

00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:56,430
The only ones that tend not to dissipate is gluten because there's so much hidden gluten in stuff.

00:02:57,070 --> 00:03:02,990
So, you know, many times people with a gluten sensitivity have to stay off gluten for their life.

00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:09,950
If you have, we do a Cyrex-10 and you have other foods that show up in the yellow or in the red,

00:03:09,950 --> 00:03:16,190
that's the equivocal or in the out of range, red. And you stay away from those for even three

00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:23,470
months and you did the test again, those could be gone. So looking back at a test that you did six

00:03:23,470 --> 00:03:32,670
plus months ago, it's kind of a mute point. If I had antibodies in the equivocal range to any food

00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:41,470
six months ago, I would hesitate eating it now. If I had stayed away, if I've never stayed away from

00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:47,550
them once and I was eating it every day, even after getting that test done, then you probably still have

00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:53,870
antibodies that it might even be in the out of range, red zone. But if you stayed away from those

00:03:53,870 --> 00:04:01,790
for the most part, they may be all gone. So it's kind of what you look at a test. It's like looking at a

00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:06,910
blood test that you did eight months ago and making clinical decisions off that your body's changed.

00:04:08,110 --> 00:04:15,710
It's not worth looking at the test, except to know trends, your body's changed. So I would not make

00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:22,910
any clinical decisions based upon a food sensitivity test done more than a month or so ago, because your

00:04:22,910 --> 00:04:24,510
body changes.

